    "extracted text": "The ITH-zeotype germanosilicates were synthesized under hydrothermal conditions using TMHDA as an OSDA. In a typical synthesis, 4 mL of TMHDA and 0.0262 g GeO2 were added to 0.81 mL water. The mixture was stirred using a magnetic stirrer until the germanium oxide was dissolved. After adding 0.1 mL of TEOS, the mixture was stirred for 30 min at room temperature to hydrolyze the TEOS, followed by the addition of 0.057 mL of an aqueous HF solution. The molar ratio of the batch composition was 0.5GeO2: 1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O. The final mixture (pH 7-8) was sealed in a 25-mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated to 170 °C under autogenous pressure for 7 days. All the samples were synthesized at 170 °C for 7 days. As for the synthesis of Co and Cu-containing ITH, CoCl2·6H2O and CuCl2·2H2O were used as the precursors, respectively, and added into the reaction gel to obtain the following molar composition: 0.5GeO2:1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O:0.15CoO or 0.10 CuO.",
    
    "property mapping": "Si - represented as SiO2 in the table and text\nGe - represented as GeO2 in the table and text\nMeO - represents either CuO or CoO (transition metal oxides)\nH2O - water in the reaction mixture\nTMHDA - represents N,N,N',N'-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine, the organic structure-directing agent (OSDA)\nHF - hydrofluoric acid\nProducts - resulting zeolite structure (ITH, Cu-ITH, Co-ITH or amorphous)",
    
    "formula abbreviations": "TMHDA stands for N,N,N',N'-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine, which is the organic structure-directing agent (OSDA).\nTEOS stands for tetraethyl orthosilicate, which is the silicon source.\nMeO stands for either CuO or CoO, depending on whether copper or cobalt is being incorporated into the zeolite.",
    
